+# [FIX] No cache mount on build/ meant every change to src/services/
+# static_config.yaml invalidated this layer and forced a full from-scratch
+# recompile+relink of all 4 binaries (observed repeatedly: full CXX compiler
+# identification + every .o rebuilt, 10+ minutes each time) — a BuildKit
+# cache mount persists CMake/Ninja's incremental build state across builds
+# independently of layer invalidation, so only changed translation units
+# actually get recompiled/relinked. /install stays a normal (non-cache) path
+# so `cmake --install` output still lands in the image layer for the
+# COPY --from=builder steps below to pick up.
+RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/src/build,sharing=locked \
+    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/install \
